      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3901997793",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "`IsDummyEmail` treats any string containing '@' as eligible for dummy-domain checking, so values like \"@U18.virgin.com\" (empty local part) are classified as dummy emails. This can incorrectly set `HoHManaged=true` and change email/template behaviour. Consider validating the separator position and trimming whitespace (similar to `EmailRecipientPolicy.ShouldSuppress`).",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Updated IsDummyEmail to trim the address and reject a missing local part or domain before comparing the configured dummy domain. Added focused malformed-address tests proving HoHManaged remains false."
    },
    {
      "threadId": "PRRT_kwDORKRjBc6eBKKz",
      "replyToCommentDatabaseId": 3901997825,
      "path": "docs/behavior-harness.md",
      "line": 70,
      "url": "https://github.com/VAAD1ST/eapi/pull/1731#discussion_r3901997825",
      "author": "copilot-pull-request-reviewer",
      "body": "This table is for planned/implemented flow status, but this row marks `vaa-eapi-myaccount-under18-enrolment` as `Ready` while the sequence-diagram index lists it as `InProgress` and the diagram itself is `InProgress`. Aligning the status here avoids conflicting docs about the flow state.",
      "decision": "valid",
      "resolutionComment": "Aligned the planned behavior entry to InProgress, matching both the diagram Agent Loop Goal and the sequence-diagram index. No sequence-diagram lifecycle status changed."
    }
